    "campaign": "WORLD OF WINE",
    "caption": "Rainy days have a way of making us want to stay home, don’t they? So if you find yourself hungry for a bowl of comfort, then try this easy Butternut Squash soup recipe. It takes just 30 minutes to make, and pairs well with good bread and a glass of Mi Mi en Provence Grande Réserve Rosé. This lovely pink wine’s flowery notes and subtle fruit flavors will have you feeling like you’re in a quaint countryside cafe in France–even if it’s pouring outside.  \n\nServing time: 30 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\n\nIngredients\n2 tbsps. olive oil\n7 cups butternut squash, diced\n1 pc. white onion\nsalt and pepper to taste\n2 cups chicken stock\n1 cup heavy cream\nSalt and pepper to taste\n2 tbsps. butter\n1 cup bacon\n2 tbsps. dill\nMi Mi en Provence Grande Réserve Rosé\n\nProcedure\nSet pot over medium heat. Add olive oil and add 6 cups butternut squash and onions. Sauté for 5 minutes. Season with salt and pepper.\nAdd chicken stock, and let it boil until squash is completely tender.\nBlend squash using an immersion blender. Add in heavy cream, and let simmer for 5 minutes.\nSet a pan over medium heat, and add butter and remaining butternut squash. Cook until tender, then set aside.\nIn the same pan, cook bacon until crispy, set aside.\nTransfer to a bowl, and top with cooked butternut squash and crispy bacon. Drizzle with heavy cream and garnish with dill.\nServe alongside Mi Mi en Provence Grande Réserve Rosé.\n\nStuck at home? You can now order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
