    "caption": "Delight your guests with this simple, yet sumptuous Mushroom and Goat’s cheese crostini. This aromatic appetizer looks like it came straight out of your favorite tapas restaurant, so don’t be surprised if it gets finished quickly. \n\nPair this umami bomb of a starter with the equally bold Penfolds Koonunga Hill Cabernet Sauvignon. It’s full-bodied with the right balance of savory and spice, while retaining excellent structure in the palate. Glasses of this excellent red wine will fuel great conversations well into the night. \n\nServing time: 20 minutes\nYield: 6 servings\n\nIngredients\n1 pc. baguette, sliced\n2 tbsps. butter\n1 tbsp. olive oil\n2 cups shimeji mushroom\n2 cups shiitake mushroom\nsalt and pepper to taste\n1 cup goat cheese\n½ cup thyme sprigs\nPenfolds Koonunga Hill Cabernet Sauvignon\n\nProcedure\nToast baguette until nicely golden, then set aside.\nSet a pan over medium heat. Add butter and olive oil, then sauté shimeji mushrooms and shiitake mushrooms. Season with salt and pepper. Set aside.\nSpread goat cheese over crostinis. Top with sautéed mushrooms.\nGarnish with thyme sprigs. Serve alongside Penfolds Koonunga Hill Cabernet Sauvignon.\n\nReady to restock your pantry? Order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
