    "campaign": "WORLD OF WINE",
    "caption": "Looking for a comforting home-cooked meal? You can’t go wrong with classics like Chicken Cacciatore. It’s hearty, tangy and sure to make anyone eating it feel like getting a tight hug. And while it does take a while to get ready, it’s well worth the effort–just like all good things are.\n\nPair this delicious meal with the 19 Crimes Cabernet Sauvignon. This intense red wine is great for both cooking and drinking. It’s firm and full on the palate, with a subtle sweetness and flavors that hint of red currants, dark cherries, and chocolate. \n\nServing time: 50 minutes\nYield: 4-6 servings\n\nIngredients\nSalt and pepper to taste\n1kg bone-in chicken cut-ups\n3 tbsps. olive oil\n2 tbsps. butter\n1 white onion, diced \n5 cloves garlic, minced \n1 red bell pepper, diced \n½ cup mushrooms, sliced \n2 tsps. dried oregano\n2 tbsps. tomato paste\n½ cup 19 Crimes Cabernet Sauvignon \n2 cups crushed tomatoes \n½ cup chicken stock \n\nProcedure\nSeason chicken cut-ups with salt and pepper. \nPreheat a large pot over medium high heat, then add in olive oil. Sear chicken until nicely browned and caramelized on both sides. Do this in batches to avoid overcrowding the pan. Set aside chicken while retaining the oil. \nAdd in butter, then sweat onions, garlic, bell peppers and mushrooms until soft and aromatic. Mix in dried oregano and tomato paste, then cook until paste is slightly darkened. \nAdd back seared chicken cut-ups, and pour in 19 Crimes Cabernet Sauvignon. Let the wine reduce to half.  \nMix in crushed tomatoes and chicken stock. Let simmer for 12-15 minutes.\nEnjoy with the rest of the 19 Crimes Cabernet Sauvignon.\n\nGet your pantry stocked for your next date night at home. Order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
