    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "WORLD OF WINE",
    "caption": "Who says you can’t make a gourmet pizza at home? With great ingredients, and some clever kitchen hacks, you too can make this fancy Steak and Blue Cheese Pizza–even if you’re not a skilled baker. The secret is puff pastry: it’s a great shortcut to pizza dough.\n\nAs you’d expect, a proper red wine cuts through the meaty and creamy flavors of these toppings well. We suggest the Beronia Rioja Crianza for this, as it has a fresh herbaceous aroma, and complex flavors that suggest vanilla, milk chocolate, and American oak.\n\nServing time: 1 hour\nYield: 3-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n1 slab sirloin steak \nSalt and pepper to taste \n2 tbsps. olive oil \n2 tbsps. butter\n2 white onions, sliced \n1 sheet puff pastry\n1 cup marinara sauce \n1 cup mozzarella cheese, grated \n½ cup blue cheese, crumbled\n1 cup arugula \nBeronia Rioja Crianza  \n\nProcedure\nPat-dry sirloin steak, then season with salt and pepper on both sides. \nHeat up a cast iron pan over high heat, then add in olive oil. Once smoking, sear steak until you achieve a nicely browned crust. Reduce heat to medium, then add in butter, and baste for 2-3 minutes, or until your desired doneness. For medium doneness, remove steak when the internal temperature reaches 130C. Let rest covered with foil for 5-8 minutes. \nIn the same pan with remaining fat, sweat onions until super soft and caramelized, about 10 minutes. Preheat oven to 180C. \nPrick holes all over the puff pastry sheet. Spread marinara sauce, then top with mozzarella cheese. Bake for 20-22 minutes, or until puff pastry is golden brown. \nTop with caramelized onions, sliced sirloin steak, blue cheese and arugula. \nEnjoy with Beronia Rioja Crianza.\n \nExcited to make more great dishes at home? Then order your groceries online now at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
