    "caption": "Lamb Chops aren’t the most popular sight in our pork-crazy country, but they really should be. They’re easy to cook, and have a robust, mildly gamey flavor that’s quite delicious when grilled with dijon mustard and fresh herbs. Try this easy recipe for a restaurant quality meal at home!\nAnd make sure to complement this delicious dish with a bold wine like Hardys The Riddle Cabernet Merlot. It has a good, fruit intensity of dark plum and cassis on the palate, well integrated oak notes, and a soft, velvety finish that lingers nicely. \n\nServing time: 45 minutes\nYield: 2 servings\n\nIngredients\n3 tbsps. olive oil \n2 tsps. dijon mustard \n4 cloves garlic, minced \n2 tbsps. rosemary, chopped\n2 tsps. lemon juice\nSalt and pepper to taste\n\n3 tbsps. olive oil\n4 pcs. lamb chops, frenched\nHardys The Riddle Cabernet Merlot\n\nProcedure\nWhisk together olive oil, dijon mustard, garlic, rosemary and lemon juice. Season with salt and pepper to taste. \nMarinate lamb chops in this mixture for at least 30 minutes, or ideally overnight. \nPreheat a grill pan over medium-high heat. Add in olive oil. Once smoking, sear lamb chops for 3 minutes on each side. \nEnjoy with Hardys The Riddle Cabernet Merlot. \n\nReady to try this hearty pairing? Order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
