    "campaign": "WORLD OF WINE",
    "caption": "In the mood for some slow cooking this weekend? This Braised Beef Short Ribs recipe is a great choice. Yes, it takes 3.5 hours to make, but don’t fret; most of that is just a slow-braise. You can watch episodes of your favorite shows while waiting for the sauce to deepen in flavor, and the meat to to get fall-off-the-bone tender. \n\nThis recipe calls for red wine, and we recommend the Lapis Luna Cabernet Sauvignon for this. A classic Cabernet, it has the characteristic full bodied taste and balanced acidity associated with this region’s grapes. \n\nServing time: 3 hours and 30 minutes\nYield: 4-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n1kg bone-in beef short ribs \nSalt and pepper to taste\n3 tbsps. olive oil \n2 tbsps. butter\n1 white onion, diced\n2 celery ribs, chopped\n5 cloves garlic, chopped\n2 tbsps. tomato paste\n2 sprigs fresh thyme \n2 bay leaves\n3 cups beef broth \n1 cup Lapis Luna Cabernet Sauvignon\n2 tbsps. worcestershire sauce\n\nProcedure\nPat-dry beef short ribs, then season with salt and pepper. \nPreheat a large pot over medium-high heat, then add in olive oil. Once smoking, sear beef short ribs until nicely browned on all sides. Do this in batches. Set aside beef while retaining oil in the pan. \nIn the same pan, sweat onions, celery and garlic in butter until soft and aromatic. Mix in tomato paste, and cook until slightly darkened. \nAdd in thyme, bay leaves, beef broth, Lapis Luna Cabernet Sauvignon and worcestershire sauce. Let boil. Add back seared beef short ribs, then bring down to a simmer. Cover, and let cook over low heat for 2-3 hours, or until meat is fork-tender. \nTransfer beef short ribs to a serving plate, while leaving the broth in the pan. Let reduce to your desired thickness, then pour over the beef. \nServe with Lapis Luna Cabernet Sauvignon. \n\nYou can now order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
