    "caption": "Bolognese is one of the world’s most beloved comfort foods. But even without an Italian grandma’s family recipe, you can easily make a great sauce at home. All you need is a little patience and some good red wine to create that deep, slow-cooked flavor. \nFor this classic pasta dish, we recommend the Montes Alpha Cabernet Sauvignon. A leader among Chilean Cabernets, this bottling is as great in a meat sauce as it is in a wine glass. It boasts great complexity with its full bodied structure, well-balanced flavor and long finish.  \n\nServing time: 2 hours\nYield: 4-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n2 tbsps. olive oil \n4 cloves garlic, minced\n1 white onion, minced\n1 carrot, grated\n2 celery ribs, chopped \n½ kg ground beef \n½ cup Montes Alpha Cabernet Sauvignon\n2 tbsps. tomato paste\n2 cups crushed tomatoes \n½ cup whole milk\n¾ cup beef stock\n2 sprigs fresh oregano \n½ cup parmesan cheese\n¼ cup basil leaves, chopped\n\nProcedure\nIn large pot, heat up olive oil over medium heat. Sweat garlic, onions, carrots and celery until soft and aromatic. Add in beef, and cook until nicely browned. \nPour in Montes Alpha Cabernet Sauvignon, and let cook until wine has reduced to half. \nMix in tomato paste, crushed tomatoes, whole milk, beef stock and oregano. Reduce heat to lowest setting, and let cook for 1 hour while stirring occasionally. \nOnce beef is very tender, mix in parmesan cheese, then season with salt and pepper to taste. Turn off heat, then mix in basil leaves. \nServe over your preferred pasta, and enjoy with Montes Alpha Cabernet Sauvignon. \n\nYou can now order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
