    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "WORLD OF WINE",
    "caption": "Nothing brightens up a good steak like fresh chimichurri. Its spicy, tangy, and herby notes cut through the beef's richness well, making it a great condiment for meat lovers. This Argentinian staple is super easy to make, and ages well too. Make sure to save some, as aged chimichurri develops wonderful depth of flavor in just a few days. \n\nFor this steak recipe, we recommend pairing it with the Château Grand Monteil 2019 Bordeaux Superior. It’s savory, slightly acidic, and light-bodied, so it doesn’t overwhelm the chimichurri at all. \n\nServing time: 45 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\n\nIngredients\n1 slab rib-eye steak (1-inch thick), at room temperature\nSalt and pepper to taste \n2 tbsps. olive oil \n2 tbsps. butter \n2 cloves garlic \n1 sprig thyme \nChâteau Grand Monteil 2019 Bordeaux Superior \nCHIMICHURRI: \n1 shallot, minced \n1 green chili, minced\n3 cloves garlic, minced \n¼ cup red wine vinegar \n½ cup cilantro, chopped\n¼ cup parsley, chopped\n½ cup extra virgin olive oil\nSalt and pepper to taste\n\nProcedure\nPat dry rib-eye steak, then season with salt and pepper on both sides.  \nPreheat a cast-iron grill pan over high heat, then add in olive oil. Once smoking, sear rib-eye steak until a nicely brown crust forms. Flip over to sear the other side, then reduce heat to medium, and add butter, garlic and thyme. Baste steak for 2-3 minutes, or until your desired doneness. For medium doneness, remove steak when its internal temperature reaches 130C. Let rest covered with foil for 5-8 minutes. \nCombine shallots, green chili, garlic and red wine vinegar. Let sit for 3 minutes to soften the aromatics. Mix in the rest of the chimichurri ingredients. \nServe steak with chimichurri and enjoy with Château Grand Monteil 2019 Bordeaux Superior. \n\nYou can now order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Come and join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber",
